Dear Altuna,
I realize that people have been analyzing methylation by looking at it under different context. I know that other methylation analysis software also analyse the data in such a manner. So I do realize that it is standard practice. However, I would like to test to see what happens in my dataset when I do not segregate the analysis into CpG and non-CpG context. I believe that this is the purpose of research. It wouldn't be research if we just followed what everyone else is saying or doing.

Thanks once again for your input.

Best,
Jingxian

